<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Hatfield Chase</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">633</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Hatfield Chase was fought in 633 near Doncaster in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yorkshire">Yorkshire</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cadwallon-ap-cadfan">Cadwallon ap Cadfan</a> of Gwynedd and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda of Mercia</a> defeated and killed Edwin, the Christian king of Northumbria. Northumbria split into its two kingdoms of Deira and Bernicia and was ravaged by Cadwallon for a year, until Oswald defeated him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-heavenfield">Battle of Heavenfield</a> in 634.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-hatfield-chase.jpg" alt="Battle of Hatfield Chase" width="320" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: F. H. Townsend · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Death_of_Edwin_of_Northumbria_at_Hatfield_-_F._H._Townsend.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
